[234.820566, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[5Gnot\u001b[9Ga\u001b[11Gservice,\u001b[20Gso\u001b[23Git\u001b[26Gstops\u001b[32Gon\u001b[35Greboot.\u001b[43GTo\u001b[46Gbring\u001b[52Git\u001b[55Gback,\u001b[61Grun\u001b[65G\u001b[38;5;153mPATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH\" bash \r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B~/mash-setup-dl/mash-local-nats-setup.sh --dir ~/mash-nats --start\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G- \u001b[1mPlugin:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;5;153mmash@mash\u001b[39m is \u001b[28Gstalled, wi\u001b[40Gh\u001b[42Gone MCP serv\u001b[55Gr and the three expected hooks. It loads in\u001b[99Gyour next\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  Claude\u001b[12GCode\u001b[17Gsession.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5G\u001b[1mMailboxes:\u001b[16G\u001b[22mBoth\u001b[21Gendpoints\u001b[31Gshow\u001b[36G\u001b[38;5;153mready\u001b[39m.\u001b[43GA\u001b[45Gtest\u001b[50Gmessage\u001b[58Gfrom\u001b[63Gbob\u001b[67Gto\u001b[70Galice\u001b[76Garrived\u001b[84Gwith\u001b[89G\u001b[38;5;153mtrust: verified\u001b[39m.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B- \u001b[1mLaunchers:\u001b[22m \u001b[38;5;153mbob\u001b[39m and\u001b[24G\u001b[38;5;153malice\u001b[30G\u001b[39min\u001b[33G\u001b[38;5;153m~/.local/bin\u001b[46G\u001b[39meach\u001b[51Gstart\u001b[57GClaude\u001b[64GCode\u001b[69Gas\u001b[72Gthat\u001b[77Gagent,\u001b[84Gwith\u001b[89Gthe\u001b[93Gdevelopment\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bchannel\u001b[13Gflag\u001b[18Gyou\u001b[22Gchose.\u001b[29GClaude\u001b[36GCode\u001b[41Gwill\u001b[46Gshow\u001b[51Ga\u001b[53Gwarning\u001b[61Gscreen\u001b[68Gto\u001b[71Gconfirm\u001b[79Gat\u001b[82Geach\u001b[87Gstart.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mYour turn:\u001b[14G\u001b[22mrun\u001b[18Geach\u001b[23Gof\u001b[26Gthese\u001b[32Gin\u001b[35Gits\u001b[39Gown\u001b[43Gterminal:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2Bbob\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Balice\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BEach should say which\u001b[25Gagent it is and that mail wakes\u001b[57Git when idle. Then run \u001b[38;5;153mmash inbox\u001b[39m i\u001b[93G a\u001b[96Gice's session.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BNote that\u001b[13Gthe\u001b[17Gtest\u001b[22Gmessage\u001b[30GI\u001b[32Gsent\u001b[37Gis\u001b[40Galready\u001b[48Gin\u001b[51Galice's\u001b[59Ginbox.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GTo g\u001b[8Gve\u001b[11Gthe\u001b[15Gpair a first job, p\u001b[35Gste this into\u001b[49Gthe \u001b[38;5;153mbob\u001b[39m session:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;153mBob, you are the lead coordinator for this pair programming team and today we\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwill be working on a basic Hello World in Rust. Alice is your peer and she'll\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbe taking a look at your code and making suggestions. This Hello World needs\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsolid code coverage. Maybe it's best if Alice writes the tests. Talk to Alice\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band come up with a plan.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;5;246m✻\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;246mBrewed for 1m 27s ·\u001b[23Gdone 8:06 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[3B❯ \r\u001b[38C\u001b[2B\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
